"""bikehook_solidworks: SolidWorks feature tree of the bike hook (bikehook.stl), generated by stl2cad (bikehook_src/gen_sw.py
from bikehook_exact.py). Calls checked with sw_probe_hook.py, sw_probe_hook2.py, sw_probe_hook3.py (SolidWorks 2025).

Feature tree (model coordinates = SolidWorks coordinates; Front Plane = xy, Top Plane = xz):
  Bosses         six circles on a plane at z = 2.5, Extruded Boss mid-plane 5 mm;
  Cradle         J path (lines, R15 arcs) on the Top Plane; tapered section (lines, tangent arcs) on a plane at the
                 leg's top end; Sweep;
  Rib            outline on the Top Plane, Extruded Boss mid-plane 26 mm; Rib fillet R1.5 on its bottom edges
                 (picked by a point on each); End fillet R1.9 on every edge of the two end faces;
  Trunk n        Loft between consecutive horizontal sections (12 corners, tangent arcs) on planes parallel to the
                 Front Plane, with a guide line (3D sketch) joining corner 0 of the two sections; if its volume is
                 off, again with guide lines at all corners, then without guides;
  Arm n          curved member: a 3D sketch spline (CreateSpline2, natural ends) through its points; planes normal to
                 the spline at its points (at most 7 mm apart); an ellipse on each; Loft through the ellipses with
                 the spline as centerline (else without it, else a loft between each pair as CadQuery has it);
  Top cut, Tyre cut, Holes   Cut-Extrudes mid-plane through the part (SolidWorks makes no feature for a cut
                 that removes nothing: the top cut, when no arm reaches above the bosses);
  Junction fillet  R_FILLET on the edges where the arms meet the trunk, the bosses, the cradle and each other
                 (not in the CadQuery model: OCC cannot fillet them).
Sketches (DIMENSION = True): the outlines fully defined by stl2cad's sketch plan (relations and dimensions, no
redundancy; symmetric outlines about a centerline); circles by diameter and centre; each arm ellipse by its centre
pierced by the spline, the major-axis end's horizontal and vertical distances and the minor semi-axis; the arm
splines' points fixed (SolidWorks takes no z dimension in a 3D sketch: edit them by their X, Y, Z); the trunk guide
lines' ends coincident with their sections' corners.
After every feature the volume and centre of mass are compared with CadQuery's values (STEPS); each feature's
own change is checked, the small differences of earlier features carried.

Needs: Windows, SolidWorks, Python with pywin32.   Run: python bikehook_solidworks.py [C:\\path\\part.SLDPRT]
"""
